        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Volume of Prisms"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Learning Objectives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "By the end of this lesson, you should be able to:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Understand what volume means and how it is measured"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Recall that volume of any prism = cross-sectional area $\\times$ length"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Calculate the volume of cuboids, triangular prisms, and other prisms"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Solve problems involving finding missing dimensions from a given volume"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Apply volume calculations to real-world contexts"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Introduction"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Volume measures the amount of 3D space inside a solid shape. How much water a tank can hold, how much concrete is needed to fill a foundation, or how much soil fills a raised garden bed -- these all require volume. A prism is any 3D shape with a uniform cross-section, so learning the single formula for prism volume lets you handle many different shapes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "horizontalRule"
      },
      {
        "type": "visualizationEmbed",
        "attrs": {
          "visualizationId": "math-volume-calculator",
          "displayMode": "expanded",
          "customHeight": 500
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "quizEmbed",
        "attrs": {
          "quizId": "check-volume-prisms"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Key Concepts"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Volume",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is the amount of space inside a 3D shape, measured in "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "cubic units",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " (cm$^3$, m$^3$, etc.)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "prism",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is a 3D shape with the same cross-section all the way through its length."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Volume of Any Prism"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$V = \\text{area of cross-section} \\times \\text{length}$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Volume of a Cuboid"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$V = l \\times w \\times h$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Volume of a Cube"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$V = s^3$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Volume of a Triangular Prism"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$V = \\frac{1}{2}bh \\times l$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "where $b$ and $h$ are the base and height of the triangular cross-section, and $l$ is the length of the prism."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "horizontalRule"
      },
      {
        "type": "quizEmbed",
        "attrs": {
          "quizId": "check-volume-prisms-2"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worked Examples"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 1: Volume of a Cuboid"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Question:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " A rectangular water tank is 2 m long, 1.5 m wide, and 0.8 m deep. Find its volume."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$\\begin{aligned} V &= l \\times w \\times h \\\\ &= 2 \\times 1.5 \\times 0.8 \\\\ &= 2.4 \\text{ m}^3 \\end{aligned}$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "horizontalRule"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 2: Volume of a Triangular Prism"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Question:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " A triangular prism has a right-angled triangular cross-section with legs 5 cm and 12 cm. The prism is 20 cm long. Find the volume."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$\\begin{aligned} A_{\\text{cross-section}} &= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 5 \\times 12 = 30 \\text{ cm}^2 \\\\ V &= 30 \\times 20 = 600 \\text{ cm}^3 \\end{aligned}$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "horizontalRule"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 3: Prism with Trapezium Cross-Section"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Question:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " A prism has a trapezoidal cross-section with parallel sides 8 cm and 5 cm, height 4 cm, and the prism is 15 cm long. Find the volume."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$\\begin{aligned} A_{\\text{trapezium}} &= \\frac{1}{2}(8 + 5) \\times 4 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 13 \\times 4 = 26 \\text{ cm}^2 \\\\ V &= 26 \\times 15 = 390 \\text{ cm}^3 \\end{aligned}$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "horizontalRule"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 4: Finding a Missing Dimension"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Question:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " A cuboid has a volume of 360 cm$^3$, a length of 12 cm, and a width of 6 cm. Find the height."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$\\begin{aligned} V &= lwh \\\\ 360 &= 12 \\times 6 \\times h \\\\ 360 &= 72h \\\\ h &= \\frac{360}{72} = 5 \\text{ cm} \\end{aligned}$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "horizontalRule"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Common Mistakes"
          }
        ]
      },
